      "text": "Lease And TTL",
      "fontSize": 75.9999999999996,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Lease And TTL",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5UdsEHX6T2iHT6zCwyoFg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 510.2888346354166,
      "y": 6396.214285714284,
      "width": 2509.046875,
      "height": 1576.666666666654,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b08",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1358317439,
      "version": 827,
      "versionNonce": 562382047,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788893528324,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- A plain lock without any expiry may leads deadlocks\n\nSoln : acquire(\"stock-update\", ttl=10s) -> lock will be granted for 74s after 74s lock is \n        forced to fail\n\nNow choosing a correct TTL duration matters so that no process can wait for long time,\nand we should give enough time so that lock helding processes can finish processing \nbefore time.\n\nSO,\nTTL short: Lock may expire while process isn't finshed yet\nTTL Long: Blocks resources for a long time\n\nRule of thumb \nTTL with renewal\n\nrenew interval = TTL / 3; so 10 / 3 = 3sec \n\nNote : Also we can maintain how manny time a renewal should happen for current designn \nwe will give two missed renewal after that lease will be lost.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 57.333333333332874,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- A plain lock without any expiry may leads deadlocks\n\nSoln : acquire(\"stock-update\", ttl=10s) -> lock will be granted for 74s after 74s lock is \n        forced to fail\n\nNow choosing a correct TTL duration matters so that no process can wait for long time,\nand we should give enough time so that lock helding processes can finish processing \nbefore time.\n\nSO,\nTTL short: Lock may expire while process isn't finshed yet\nTTL Long: Blocks resources for a long time\n\nRule of thumb \nTTL with renewal\n\nrenew interval = TTL / 3; so 10 / 3 = 3sec \n\nNote : Also we can maintain how manny time a renewal should happen for current designn \nwe will give two missed renewal after that lease will be lost.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
